### 2026-08-15T23:51:57.329Z | claude (claude-sonnet-5) | claude | conversation 627637ca-d250-4ad7-8a24-ddd841e171dd

Two different things, and they don't line up — that mismatch is exactly the shape of gap that bit Melody:

- **The app itself** doesn't need anything in `invariants.spec.js` to work — a new mode just needs its own `data-mode="..."` option and JS module, same as always.
- **Most other invariant tests auto-include it for free** — INV-1, INV-3's follow-up, INV-9/12, INV-11, and the reachability half of INV-13 all call a shared `getModes(page)` helper that reads `data-mode` attributes live off the DOM, so a new mode is automatically swept in with zero maintenance.
- **[REDACTED_SECRET] does NOT.** `[REDACTED_PRIVATE_INFO]` (`[REDACTED_PRIVATE_INFO]`) is a hand-written array — each entry needs its own `mutate()` function (a real UI interaction that changes that mode's state), which can't be auto-derived since every mode's "do something" gesture is different. Add a new mode without touching this array, and [REDACTED_SECRET] simply never tests it — no failure, no warning, nothing. That's precisely how Melody went unchecked for as long as it did, just with the omission moved one level up (missing from a list, rather than a wrong claim about that list).
- The same is true of `[REDACTED_PRIVATE_INFO]`, and separately `PRIMARY_ELEMENTS`/`SECONDARY_ELEMENTS`/`CONTAINER_ID` for INV-13's coverage-nudge test — all hand-maintained per-mode maps, none derived from `getModes()`.

So the honest answer to "will I need to update anything": yes, `[REDACTED_PRIVATE_INFO]` (+ `[REDACTED_PRIVATE_INFO]` if the mode has a meaningful counter) — but the test suite won't tell you to. Want me to build a coverage-nudge check for this too, the same pattern used for INV-13 (fail loud if a mode from `getModes()` is missing from `[REDACTED_PRIVATE_INFO]`), so this stops depending on remembering?


### 2026-08-15T23:53:25.506Z | claude (sonnet) | user | conversation 627637ca-d250-4ad7-8a24-ddd841e171dd

